  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed for both practical independence (financial, residential) and psychological maturity. A key concept in Japanese discussions about adulthood and social welfare.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {経済的|けいざいてき}{自立|じりつ}: financial independence\n- {精神的|せいしんてき}{自立|じりつ}: emotional/psychological independence\n- {自立|じりつ}した{生活|せいかつ}: independent life\n- {自立|じりつ}{支援|しえん}: independence support\n- {自立|じりつ}{心|しん}: spirit of independence\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {自律|じりつ}: self-discipline, autonomy — focuses on governing oneself and one's actions, whereas {自立|じりつ} focuses on being able to support oneself independently\n- {独立|どくりつ}: independence — broader term that also applies to nations and organizations",
